note: "Round 1 of Tier-3 review returned FAIL with three verified findings (a Checkbox tier self-contradiction, a miscounted and misattributed <ol>, a broken anchor); fixing them surfaced two more (a missed caption still counting two build-local compositions, and a lexicon violation naming the proven-decrypted milestone \"the verify step\"). Round 3 on the committed tip found three more, one of them introduced by round 2's own fix (the lexicon swap kept the forbidden verb 'working'), plus a 'nine entries reused' count that contradicted its own catalog and a stale build-local prediction in the plan. Round 4 found four more, including a real gap in the artifact's evidence: the ok-toned Notice the run specifies was asserted in four stages and mounted in none, so the string two earlier rounds had fought over existed only in prose. It now mounts beside step 2's unproven verdict. Also a Checkbox warrant citing SegmentedControl's @avoid for a phrase that is its @use, a stale 'nine verdicts' estimate in the plan where the run measured sixteen, and a third stale build-local prediction. Rounds 5 and 6 corrected the fix itself twice more: round 4 mounted the ok-toned Notice in a step with no Button, round 5 moved it beside a disabled button (which Button's @avoid allows only next to a progress line), round 6 rendered step 2's done state as SetProxy ships it, and round 7 — an independent pass once the rate limit lifted — caught that the review row claimed the mute remedy beside it also came from Onboarding.tsx when it is this run's design, unbuilt until StepStatusView.short lands. The design was right; the claim about it was false, and both the review row and the mockup caption now say which mounted element is designed rather than shipped. Seventeen defects across six rounds, all recorded in the run's own review table, which keeps the three-attempt account rather than presenting the final placement as the first. Separately, nine verify-doc failures were found and fixed before this note was written, none of which my hand-checks had caught: data-key slugs must be kebab-case (copy-text, not copytext) or four components resolve to nothing and the mockup reads as hand-drawn; two supporting tables sat inside data-item=elements, so the gist predicate demanded a gist on all 30 rows; three review rows cited their contract in prose rather than <code>, and the blind-run row named no stage (now `nothing`, the sanctioned answer); the mockup's own .a-stage CSS hand-wrote letter-spacing .04em instead of tracking-label, breaking both type-tokens-only and uppercase-mute-labels; and the data-wire element needed font-mono on itself. Recorded because the earlier claim in this session that the cargo gates could not run here was wrong — cargo is absent from PATH but present via $HOME/.cargo/env, which the hooks source."
